From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Santiago Palladino <santiago@aztec-labs.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:55:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] test(e2e): simplify the registry reduction calculator rewards
 test

Reads the proven checkpoints through the node API instead of the archiver,
attributes each one to its header coinbase, and tracks only the reward and fee
each coinbase has earned; the stop condition is a proven checkpoint with txs
by a validator of each kind. Drops the restated protocol invariants, the
proposer re-derivation and the fee-to-reward ratio bookkeeping. The governance
calls go through RollupCheatCodes.asOwner, the calculator is owned by the L1
deployer, and the ATP deposits move to a helper.

RollupContract.getSequencerRewards takes an optional block number so the
rewards can be read at the same L1 block as the proven tip.

